# Change: G-C and C-G7 (repertoire plan: st-change-g-c-c-g7). An original chord-change study.
# Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord held for two bars (one
# strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half (home G): G (320003) fingered 3-2-4 (3 on string 6 fret 3, 2 on string 5
# fret 2, 4 on string 1 fret 3) with C (x32010): fingers 3 and 2 keep their shape and move one
# string toward string 1, and finger 1 lands on string 2 fret 1. Second half (home C): C with
# G7 (320001): the 3-2 shape moves back one string, and finger 1 moves from string 2 fret 1 to
# string 1 fret 1. It ends G7 to C, the strongest way home. Keep the metronome on: the new chord
# lands on the beat even if the strum before it catches open strings.
title: Change: G-C and C-G7
id: st-change-g-c-c-g7
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: chord changes, strumming, metronome, shape shift
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
